  "level": 2,
  "questionLabels": [],
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A simple pendulum is placed at a place where its distance from the earth's surface is equal to the radius of the earth. If the length of the string is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, then the time period of small oscillations will be _________<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo></math>take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Acceleration due to gravity at surface of earth, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Now, at distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> from the surface of the earth, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Therefore,<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>l</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mo> </mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
